(SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE BOARD OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(OFFICE OF INVESTOR ASSISTANCE AND EDUCATION, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(SEBI/HO/OIAE/OIAE_IAD-1/P/CIR/2024/145) Tj
T*
(September 19, 2024) Tj
T*
(Online Dispute Resolution \(ODR\) Portal in the Indian Securities Market) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. SMART ODR Portal Architecture: The Securities Market Approach to Resolution Through Technology \(SMART ODR\) Portal provides a digital) Tj
T*
(ecosystem for conciliation and online arbitration of disputes between investors and listed entities or registered market intermediaries.) Tj
T*
(2. Escalation Mechanism: Investors must first lodge complaints on the SEBI SCORES portal or directly with the intermediary. If unsatisfied) Tj
T*
(with the resolution within 21 calendar days, the investor may escalate the dispute to the ODR Portal.) Tj
T*
(3. Conciliation Timelines: The appointed Conciliator shall conduct online conciliation sessions and conclude proceedings within 21 calendar) Tj
T*
(days of appointment. If conciliation succeeds, a settlement agreement signed electronically by both parties shall be binding.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 897 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Arbitration Timelines: If conciliation fails, either party may initiate online arbitration within 14 calendar days. The appointed) Tj
T*
(Arbitrator or Arbitral Tribunal shall pass an arbitral award within 30 calendar days of commencement of arbitration proceedings.) Tj
T*
(5. Fee Structure and Investor Exemption: For all claims up to rupees five lakh \(INR 5,00,000\), the investor is completely exempt from paying) Tj
T*
(conciliation and arbitration fees. The entire fee of the conciliators and arbitrators for such claims is funded by the concerned Market) Tj
T*
(Infrastructure Institutions \(Stock Exchanges and Depositories\).) Tj
T*
(6. Fast-Track Arbitration: For disputes with claim value exceeding rupees five lakh up to rupees thirty lakh, sole arbitrators conduct) Tj
T*
(summary document-based proceedings without mandatory oral hearings.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 924 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Pre-Deposit Requirement for Challenging Awards: Where a market intermediary or listed entity files an application in court) Tj
T*
(under Section 34 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 challenging an arbitral award passed in favor of an investor, it must deposit) Tj
T*
(seventy-five percent \(75 percent\) of the awarded amount with the Stock Exchange prior to filing the challenge.) Tj
T*
(8. Release of Pre-Deposit to Investor: In hardship cases, the Stock Exchange may release up to fifty percent of the pre-deposited award) Tj
T*
(amount to the investor against an indemnity bond pending the outcome of the court proceedings.) Tj
T*
(9. Enforcement of Settlement Agreements: Settlement agreements concluded during conciliation have the same legal status and effect as an) Tj
T*
(arbitral award on agreed terms under Section 73 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 819 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
